{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528099981,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","part":{"partID":"prt_1d235be6f002Rly8TefyFsaPXY","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","messageID":"msg_1d235b2730017YCL4JatEGoGeg","type":"tool","id":"call_c849889d5e384ff99b6c9802","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md, lines 1-253\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 10: reachability-and-attribution\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that record the offer and the brief on every run line, backfill the before arm, make the scorer attributable, add the Codex and DSH install steps with read-only doctor checks and measure the cold first prompt before changing it.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"reachability and attribution tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 10: reachability-and-attribution\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0.\n31: - `S` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`. `R` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`. `T` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`.\n32: - `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` (new). `OT` is `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` (new). `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n33: - `VT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `VO` is `npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `PRE` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n35: - `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, the Claude prompt hook entry.\n36: - `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`. `DI` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`. `DT` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/bundle.test.mjs`. `DR` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md`. `DA` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md`.\n37: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n38: - `RMY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml`. `SCY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`. `DCT` is `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-symlink-contract.test.cjs $DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs`.\n39: - `HR` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json`. `HS` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs`. `LCH` is `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`.\n40: - `FLOOR` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n41: \n42: Rules for every task:\n43: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a script and its test adds the behaviour and the one case that pins it.\n44: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A row whose split is `holdout` is never opened.\n45: - No worker starts a live model session. Live runs, arenas and operator steps are `[C]` tasks.\n46: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T028 checks it.\n47: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, edits `AGENTS.md` or renames `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`.\n48: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n49: \n50: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n51: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`, `$SP/summary-before.json`), T002 (`$SP/socket-key.txt`), T003 (`$SP/cold-start.mjs`, `$SP/cold-start-before.txt`). Read-only for the repository.\n52: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that the before arm in `PRE` is finished, because T017 changes what the start rate counts.\n53: - Wave 1: T004 (`OF`, `OT`), T005 (`S`, `T`), T006 (`DI`, `DT`), T007 (`CK`, `CKT`), T008 (`HW`, `HWT`), T009 (`IG`).\n54: - Wave 2: T010 (`OF`, `OT`), T011 (`S`, `T`), T012 (`IG`), T013 (`DR`, `DA`), T014 (`RMY`), T015 (`SCY`).\n55: - Wave 3: T016 (`OF`, `OT`), T017 (`S`, `T`), T018 (`$DS/README.markdown`).\n56: - Wave 4: T019 (`R`), T020 (`S`, `T`).\n57: - Wave 5: T021 (`R`), T022 (`S`, `T`).\n58: - Wave 6: T023 (`RA`).\n59: - Cold-start wave C1, only when T003 shows a fail-open: T024 (`HR`, then `HS` regenerates `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json`), T025 (`LCH`).\n60: - Cold-start wave C2: T026 (`$SP/cold-start-after.txt`).\n61: - Verification, one at a time: T027, T028.\n62: - After the phase is committed: T029, T030, T031 and T033 are coordinator tasks, T032 is a worker task that waits on T031 and T034 closes the phase.\n63: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n68: ## Phase 1: Setup\n69: \n70: - [ ] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`, `$SP/summary-before.json`). Run `FLOOR`, `TC`, `VT`, `DCT`, `node --test tests/bundle.test.mjs` in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards`, `node $HS --check` and `node $S --summary $PRE --json > $SP/summary-before.json`, and write each command with its last output line into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `TC` exits 0, `VT` reports 0 failed, `DCT` reports `fail 0`, the bundle test reports `fail 0`, `node $HS --check` exits 0 and `jq -r 'keys | join(\",\")' $SP/summary-before.json` prints the six runtimes.\n71: - [x] T002 Read how `$ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts` and `LCH` name the daemon socket under `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR`, and record whether two checkouts reach two daemons (`$SP/socket-key.txt`). Verify: the file names the function and the line that derive the socket name and ends with one word, `per-checkout` or `shared`. When it says `shared`, T016 gives each checkout its own socket directory.\n72: - [x] T003 Write `$SP/cold-start.mjs` and run it once with `--runs 5` (`$SP/cold-start-before.txt`). Each run makes a fresh directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cold-'))`, with `tmpdir` from `node:os`, pipes `{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"cwd\":\"<repository root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"cold-<n>\"}` into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory, and prints the milliseconds and the first line of `additionalContext` (or `<none>`). An optional `--warm` runs `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root <root> --format json --no-warm-only` detached with the same variable and waits 3,000 ms before the hook. After each run the script sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory, then removes the directory. The last line reads `fail-open N of 5`, where a run fails open when its first line does not start with `Advisor: live` or `Advisor: stale`. Verify: the file has six lines and its last line matches `fail-open [0-5] of 5`, `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cold-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing and `ls /tmp/system-skill-advisor | wc -l` prints the same number before and after the run. When N is 0, mark T024 to T026 `[x]` with `Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5` and the median milliseconds.\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n78: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n79: \n80: ### Wave 1\n81: - [x] T004 [P] Create `OF` with two exports. `parseOffer(head)` returns `{ offeredCommand, offeredPolicy }`: `offeredCommand` is the first match of `/\\/[a-z][a-z-]*:[a-z][a-z-]*(?: [a-z][a-z-]*)?/` in the head, or null, and `offeredPolicy` is `run`, `start` or `ask` when `(run)`, `(start)` or `(ask)` follows that match after optional spaces, or null. `replayOffer({ checkoutDir, prompt, sessionId, timeoutMs = 30000 })` runs `node <checkoutDir>/$HOOK` with `cwd` `checkoutDir` and the payload shape of T003, takes the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` and returns `parseOffer` of it with `offerError: null`, or null fields with `offerError` `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`. Create `OT` with cases for the heads `Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.`, `Advisor: live; ambiguous: /doctor:git hooks 0.82/0.12 vs sk-git 0.86/0.16 pass.`, `Advisor: live; use command-spec-kit-plan 0.82/0.16 pass.` and a `replayOffer` call on a folder with no hook, which returns `offerError` `hook_missing`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n82: - [x] T005 [P] In `commandParts` (`S`), when the name holds whitespace, keep the text before the first space as `name` and the rest as `route`, so `/doctor:git hooks` looks up `doctor/git.md`. Add one case to `T`: events that read `.skilled/commands/doctor/git.md` and then write give `startState(events, { expected_command: '/doctor:git hooks', expected_policy: 'run' }).started` true. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed.\n83: - [x] T006 [P] In `apply` (`DI`), change the advisor flag to `enabled: options.promptAdvisor !== false`. In `DT`, rename the test to `prompt advisor stays on unless its row flag is false` and assert that `preStepCount({ adapters: { promptAdvisor: true } })` equals `preStepCount()` and that `preStepCount({ adapters: { promptAdvisor: false } })` is one lower. Verify: `rg -n \"promptAdvisor !== false\" $DI` prints one line, and `node --test tests/bundle.test.mjs` in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards` reports `fail 0`.\n84: - [x] T007 [P] Create `CK` and `CKT`. `CK [--root <dir>] [--config <path>] [--json]` reads `<root>/.codex/hooks.json` and prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks` with exit 0 when it is absent. It finds the `UserPromptSubmit` group `g` and hook index `i` whose `command` contains `hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js`, or prints `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` with exit 1. It reads `--config`, else `${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml`, and looks for a header line `[hooks.state.\"<root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:<g>:<i>\"]`, with `<root>` as given or as its real path, followed by a `trusted_hash` line before the next header. Found prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` with exit 0. Otherwise it prints `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` and `repair: open /hooks in a Codex session at <root> and approve each entry`, with exit 1. A bad flag exits 2. It never prints a hash and calls no write, mkdir, rename or remove function. `CKT` covers an approved fixture, an unapproved fixture and a root with no `.codex`. Verify: `node --test $CKT` reports `pass 3` and `fail 0`, `rg -n \"writeFile|appendFile|mkdir|rename|rmSync|unlink\" $CK` prints nothing, and `shasum -a 256 ~/.codex/config.toml` prints the same digest before and after `node $CK --root .`, which prints one line starting `PASS` or `WARN`.\n85: - [x] T008 [P] Create `HW` and `HWT`. `HW --root <dir> [--json]` checks four runtimes: `claude` (`.claude/settings.json`, event `UserPromptSubmit`, marker `hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`), `codex` (`.codex/hooks.json`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js`), `cursor` (`.cursor/hooks.json`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js`) and `devin` (`.devin/hooks.v1.json`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js`). A runtime whose folder is absent is skipped. It reads the event under `hooks` or at the top level and prints `ok <runtime>` when its JSON text holds the marker, else `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, also for a missing or unreadable file. It exits 1 when any line is `hook-missing`, 0 otherwise and 2 on a bad flag or a missing root. It writes nothing. `HWT` covers a root whose `.claude/settings.json` lacks the entry, the same root with it and a root with no runtime folder. Verify: `node --test $HWT` reports `pass 3` and `fail 0`, and `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and exits 0.\n86: - [x] T009 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the line about hyphenated commands: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved. Verify: `rg -n \"codex-hooks-approved\" $IG` prints one line and `rg -c \"trusted_hash\" $IG` prints 1.\n87: \n88: ### Wave 2\n89: - [ ] T010 [P] Add `briefDelivered({ runtime, locator, loadSession })` to `OF`. For `claude` it reads `locator.transcriptPath` and returns true when a line has `type` `attachment`, `attachment.type` `hook_additional_context`, `attachment.hookEvent` `UserPromptSubmit` and content matching `/Advisor: [a-z]+[;. ]/`, false when the file loads without one and `\"unknown\"` when it cannot be read. For `pi` it loads the session and tests its records with the same pattern. Every other runtime returns `\"unknown\"`. Add three `OT` cases: a Claude fixture with the attachment, one without it and a `devin` locator. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T011 [P] In `S`, carry `wrote` (true when the run line's `changedPaths` is a non-empty array) on each scored result and add `byPolicy` to each tally block with keys `run`, `start` and `ask`, each `{ rows, capped, started, wrote }`, filled from the row's `expected_policy`. Print one text line per policy under each arm, `policy <name>: <rows> rows, <capped> capped, <started> started, <wrote> wrote`. Add one `T` case through the summary fixture. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.claude.pre.byPolicy | keys'` prints `[\"ask\",\"run\",\"start\"]`.\n91: - [ ] T012 [P] In `IG`, change `any of the six runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin or Pi` to `any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH)`, add DSH to the runtimes that spell commands with a hyphen and add one sentence: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`. Verify: `grep -ci dsh $IG` prints at least 2.\n92: - [ ] T013 [P] In `DR` section 5 and in the `prompt-advisor.mjs` row of `DA`, state that the bundle registers the prompt advisor unless its row flag is `false`, that the guards patch still writes `true` and that a lineage leaf stays without a brief. Verify: `rg -n \"unless its row flag is .false.\" $DR $DA` prints two lines and `rg -n \"Off unless\" $DA` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T014 [P] In `RMY`, add `codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"` to `upstream_assets` and one step after the `codex_hooks_installer` step: run `upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval` with `--root \"$PWD\"`. `PASS` is in sync, `WARN` sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line without counting as drift, and `SKIP` leaves STATUS unchanged. Keep every existing phrase. Verify: `rg -c \"codex_hook_approval\" $RMY` prints 2 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n94: - [ ] T015 [P] In `SCY`, add `hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"` to `upstream_assets`, add a step after the engine run that runs `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\"`, shows each `hook-missing <runtime>` line and ends with STATUS=WARN on exit 1, naming the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from Skilled's own file for that runtime into the target's file. Append to the invariant that the route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, keeping the words `check subcommand only`. Verify: `rg -c \"hook-wiring-check.cjs\" $SCY` prints at least 2 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n95: \n96: ### Wave 3\n97: - [ ] T016 [P] Add `backfillRunLog({ inPath, outPath, promptFor, replay = replayOffer, brief = briefDelivered, warm })` to `OF`. It refuses with code `same_path` when `outPath` resolves to `inPath`. It calls `promptFor(rowId)` for every line before writing, so a holdout or unknown row refuses the run with no output file. For each line it takes the checkout from `locator.projectDir`, warms each checkout once with `warm(checkoutDir)` (default: `advisor_status --workspace-root <dir> --format json --no-warm-only` through that checkout's `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`), replays the offer with session id `backfill-<rowId>`, sets `briefDelivered` and writes the line with the three fields and `offerBackfilled: true`. A line with no `projectDir` gets null fields and `offerError: 'no_checkout'`. When `$SP/socket-key.txt` says `shared`, `warm` and `replay` also set `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to one short `/tmp/ssa-bf-<n>` directory per checkout. Add `OT` cases with injected `replay`, `brief` and `warm` for a two-line log, a `no_checkout` line, a refused holdout id and `same_path`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed.\n98: - [ ] T017 [P] In `S`, keep capped runs out of the start denominator: `startRows` and `started` count uncapped start rows only, and a new `cappedStartRows` counts capped start rows. Print `capped start rows <n>` on the arm line. Add one `T` case with a capped and an uncapped start row. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.opencode.pre | {startRate, cappedStartRows}'` prints a `startRate` whose denominator plus `cappedStartRows` equals the arm's start rows in `$SP/summary-before.json`.\n99: - [ ] T018 [P] In `$DS/README.markdown`, add `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` to the tree, the script table and the read-only table, each with its flags and exit codes. Verify: `rg -c \"codex-hook-approval-check.cjs|hook-wiring-check.cjs\" $DS/README.markdown` prints at least 4.\n100: \n101: ### Wave 4\n102: - [ ] T019 In `R`, import `replayOffer` and `briefDelivered` from `OF`. In `runTurn`, after the restore and before the line is appended, call `replayOffer({ checkoutDir: PROJECT_DIR, prompt: job.prompt, sessionId })` and add `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` to the line, then add `briefDelivered` from the turn's locator (`\"unknown\"` in a dry run). Change nothing else in the turn. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0, `rg -c \"offeredCommand|offeredPolicy|briefDelivered\" $R` prints at least 3, and `node $R --print-argv claude | jq -r 'type'` prints `array`.\n103: - [ ] T020 In `S`, add `offered`, `startedOfOffered` and `offerUnknown` to each tally block. `offered` counts uncapped start rows whose line's `offeredCommand` names the row's expected command by namespace and name, `startedOfOffered` counts the started ones among them and `offerUnknown` counts uncapped start rows whose line has no `offeredCommand` key. Print `offered <X>, started <Y> of <X>, offer unknown <n>` on the arm line. Add one `T` case with an offered and a not-offered start row. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.claude.pre | {offered, startedOfOffered, offerUnknown}'` prints `{\"offered\":0,\"startedOfOffered\":0,\"offerUnknown\":12}`.\n104: \n105: ### Wave 5\n106: - [ ] T021 In `R`, add a `--backfill <run-log>` mode that needs `--out <new-log>` and calls `backfillRunLog` with a `promptFor` built from the runner's own `promptFor` and the fixture folder `resolve(dirname(<run-log>), G2_FIXTURE_DIRNAME)`. A refusal prints its code as JSON and exits 2. Add the mode to the usage text. Then write `$SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl` with two lines for row `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01`, runtime `claude`, arm `pre`, exit 0, empty `changedPaths`, the first with `locator` `{\"projectDir\":\"<absolute repository root>\"}` and the second with `locator` null, and run `node $R --backfill $SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl --out $SP/backfill-out.jsonl`. Verify: `jq -c '{offerBackfilled, briefDelivered, offerError, has: has(\"offeredCommand\")}' $SP/backfill-out.jsonl` prints `{\"offerBackfilled\":true,\"briefDelivered\":\"unknown\",\"offerError\":null,\"has\":true}` and then a line with `\"offerError\":\"no_checkout\"`, and `node $R --backfill $SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl --out $SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl` exits 2 and prints `same_path`.\n107: - [ ] T022 In `S`, after all lines are tallied, set `armIncomplete` on each runtime's arm block to true when its `runs` is lower than the largest `runs` of any runtime in the same arm, else false. End the arm's text line with `, arm incomplete` when it is true. Add one `T` case with two runtimes of two and one runs. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '[to_entries[] | select(.value.pre.armIncomplete == true) | .key]'` prints the runtimes whose `pre` run count in `$SP/summary-before.json` is below the largest.\n108: \n109: ### Wave 6\n110: - [ ] T023 In `RA`, describe the three run-line fields and that the offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn, the `--backfill` mode and its refusals, and the summary keys `offered`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerUnknown`, `cappedStartRows`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`. Verify: `rg -c \"offeredCommand|--backfill|armIncomplete|byPolicy|cappedStartRows\" $RA` prints at least 5.\n111: \n112: ### Cold-start wave C1 (only when T003 shows a fail-open)\n113: - [x] T024 Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5 with a sandboxed socket (median 431 ms), and a true cold start with no daemon alive measured fail-open 0 of 5 (median 742 ms against the 2,500 ms hook budget, `scratch/cold-arena-result.txt`). Original task: [P] In `HR`, add a hook `advisor-warm` with concern `Start the skill advisor daemon at session start so the first prompt gets a brief`, bound for `claude` at `SessionStart` group 0 slot 8 and for `codex` at `SessionStart` group 0 slot 5, each with runner `node`, script `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, args `advisor_status --workspace-root . --format json --no-warm-only`, timeout 3 and fallback `background`. Run `node $HS`. Do not edit a generated file by hand. Verify: `node $HS --check` exits 0, `jq '[.hooks.SessionStart[].hooks[] | select(.command | test(\"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status\"))] | length'` prints 1 for `.claude/settings.json` and for `.codex/hooks.json`, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- .cursor/hooks.json .devin/hooks.v1.json` prints nothing.\n114: - [x] T025 Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5 with a sandboxed socket (median 431 ms), and a true cold start with no daemon alive measured fail-open 0 of 5 (median 742 ms against the 2,500 ms hook budget, `scratch/cold-arena-result.txt`). Original task: [P] In `LCH`, set `SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS` to `750` in the daemon's environment when the launcher's own environment leaves it unset, and add the name to the list of variables passed to the daemon. Verify: `node --check $LCH` exits 0 and `rg -c \"SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS\" $LCH` prints at least 2.\n115: \n116: ### Cold-start wave C2\n117: - [x] T026 Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5 with a sandboxed socket (median 431 ms), and a true cold start with no daemon alive measured fail-open 0 of 5 (median 742 ms against the 2,500 ms hook budget, `scratch/cold-arena-result.txt`). Original task: Run `node $SP/cold-start.mjs --runs 5 --warm` (`$SP/cold-start-after.txt`). Verify: its last line reads `fail-open 0 of 5`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cold-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing. If it reads more than 0, revert T024 and T025 and mark them `[B]` with the printed line.\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n123: ## Phase 3: Verification\n124: \n125: - [ ] T027 Run every gate. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `TC` exits 0, `VT` and `VO` report 0 failed, `node --test $CKT $HWT` and `DCT` report `fail 0`, `node --test tests/bundle.test.mjs` in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards` reports `fail 0` and `node $HS --check` exits 0.\n126: - [ ] T028 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .dsh | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .dsh INSTALL-SKILLED.md .claude .codex` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n127: - [ ] T029 [C] Backfill the before arm: run `node $R --backfill $PRE --out $SP/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl` from the repository root while the six arenas under `$TMPDIR/skilled-behaviour-arenas/pre-<runtime>` still exist at commit `2920b1abef`. Verify: `wc -l` prints the same number for both files, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- $PRE` exits 0 and `jq -r '\"\\(.runtime) \\(.briefDelivered)\"' $SP/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl | sort | uniq -c` shows every `claude` and `pi` line as `true` and every `codex`, `devin`, `opencode` and `dsh` line as `unknown`.\n128: - [ ] T030 [C] Run `node $S --summary $SP/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl > $SP/summary-attributed.txt`. Verify: every arm line holds `offered`, `capped start rows` and three `policy` lines, and a runtime with fewer rows than the others ends with `arm incomplete`.\n129: - [ ] T031 [C] Codex smoke: prepare one arena at this phase's commit, have the operator open `/hooks` in a Codex session there and approve each entry, then run one row through `R` with `--runtime codex --arm smoke`. Verify: `node $CK --root <arena>` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, and the rollout at the line's `locator.transcriptPath` contains `Advisor: `.\n130: - [ ] T032 Only when T031's rollout contains the brief: in `briefDelivered` (`OF`), decide `codex` from its raw rollout in the shape T031 shows, with one `OT` case built from that shape. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed. When T031's rollout holds no brief, mark this task `[x]` with `Dropped: no Codex brief in the smoke rollout`.\n131: - [ ] T033 [C] DSH smoke: in an arena at this phase's commit, run one turn through `dsh` with one route patch and the guards patch and without the lineage patch. Verify: the stored step payload contains `Advisor: `.\n132: - [ ] T034 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n133: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n134: \n135: ---\n136: \n137: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n138: ## Completion Criteria\n139: \n140: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`, with T024 to T026 and T032 either done or marked dropped with their measured reason\n141: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n142: - [ ] The before arm is backfilled, and the attributed summary prints an offered count for every runtime\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n144: \n145: ---\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n148: ## Cross-References\n149: \n150: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n151: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n152: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n153: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n154: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: ## Verification Checklist\n159: \n160: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n161: ## Verification Protocol\n162: \n163: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n164: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n165: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n166: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n167: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n168: \n169: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n170: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n171: \n172: ---\n173: \n174: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n175: ## Pre-Implementation\n176: \n177: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers and the old-meaning summary are in `scratch/` (T001).\n178: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The coordinator confirmed the before arm is finished before wave 1 started.\n179: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] The socket key and the cold-start measurement are recorded (T002, T003).\n180: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n185: ## Code Quality\n186: \n187: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0.\n188: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id (T028).\n189: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] The two check scripts and the backfill write nothing in the home folder (T007, T028).\n190: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A failed replay yields null fields with an `offerError`, never a crash (T004).\n191: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n196: ## Testing Checklist\n197: \n198: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] The scorer and offer tests pass (T027).\n199: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The floors hold (T027).\n200: - [ ] CHK-022 [P1] The doctor contract tests, the two check tests and the DSH bundle test pass (T027).\n201: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The backfill has as many lines as its input and leaves the input unchanged (T029).\n202: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n203: \n204: ---\n205: \n206: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n207: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n208: \n209: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `measurement`: the harness reports a rate it cannot attribute.\n210: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the start rate is listed: `rg -n \"startRate|startRows\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\n211: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Every runtime with a prompt hook file is in the hook-wiring table: claude, codex, cursor and devin.\n212: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n213: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n214: \n215: ---\n216: \n217: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n218: ## Security\n219: \n220: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task reads or prints holdout prompt text, and the backfill refuses a holdout row id (T016).\n221: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] The Codex check prints no hash value (T007).\n222: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n223: \n224: ---\n225: \n226: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n227: ## Documentation\n228: \n229: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same fields and numbers.\n230: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The install guide, the DSH READMEs, the doctor scripts README and the routing-accuracy README match the code (T009, T012, T013, T018, T023).\n231: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n232: \n233: ---\n234: \n235: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n236: ## File Organization\n237: \n238: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, fixtures, measurements and the attributed log live in `scratch/` only.\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n240: \n241: ---\n242: \n243: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n244: ## Verification Summary\n245: \n246: | Category | Total | Verified |\n247: |----------|-------|----------|\n248: | P0 Items | 11 | 0/11 |\n249: | P1 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n250: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n251: \n252: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n253: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md, lines 1-253\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 10: reachability-and-attribution\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that record the offer and the brief on every run line, backfill the before arm, make the scorer attributable, add the Codex and DSH install steps with read-only doctor checks and measure the cold first prompt before changing it.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"reachability and attribution tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 10: reachability-and-attribution\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0.\n31: - `S` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`. `R` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`. `T` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`.\n32: - `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs` (new). `OT` is `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` (new). `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n33: - `VT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `VO` is `npx vitest run tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `PRE` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl`. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n35: - `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, the Claude prompt hook entry.\n36: - `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`. `DI` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs`. `DT` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/bundle.test.mjs`. `DR` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md`. `DA` is `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md`.\n37: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n38: - `RMY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml`. `SCY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml`. `DCT` is `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-symlink-contract.test.cjs $DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs`.\n39: - `HR` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/hook-registry.json`. `HS` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs`. `LCH` is `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`.\n40: - `FLOOR` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n41: \n42: Rules for every task:\n43: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a script and its test adds the behaviour and the one case that pins it.\n44: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A row whose split is `holdout` is never opened.\n45: - No worker starts a live model session. Live runs, arenas and operator steps are `[C]` tasks.\n46: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T028 checks it.\n47: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, edits `AGENTS.md` or renames `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`.\n48: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n49: \n50: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n51: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`, `$SP/summary-before.json`), T002 (`$SP/socket-key.txt`), T003 (`$SP/cold-start.mjs`, `$SP/cold-start-before.txt`). Read-only for the repository.\n52: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that the before arm in `PRE` is finished, because T017 changes what the start rate counts.\n53: - Wave 1: T004 (`OF`, `OT`), T005 (`S`, `T`), T006 (`DI`, `DT`), T007 (`CK`, `CKT`), T008 (`HW`, `HWT`), T009 (`IG`).\n54: - Wave 2: T010 (`OF`, `OT`), T011 (`S`, `T`), T012 (`IG`), T013 (`DR`, `DA`), T014 (`RMY`), T015 (`SCY`).\n55: - Wave 3: T016 (`OF`, `OT`), T017 (`S`, `T`), T018 (`$DS/README.markdown`).\n56: - Wave 4: T019 (`R`), T020 (`S`, `T`).\n57: - Wave 5: T021 (`R`), T022 (`S`, `T`).\n58: - Wave 6: T023 (`RA`).\n59: - Cold-start wave C1, only when T003 shows a fail-open: T024 (`HR`, then `HS` regenerates `.claude/settings.json` and `.codex/hooks.json`), T025 (`LCH`).\n60: - Cold-start wave C2: T026 (`$SP/cold-start-after.txt`).\n61: - Verification, one at a time: T027, T028.\n62: - After the phase is committed: T029, T030, T031 and T033 are coordinator tasks, T032 is a worker task that waits on T031 and T034 closes the phase.\n63: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n68: ## Phase 1: Setup\n69: \n70: - [ ] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`, `$SP/summary-before.json`). Run `FLOOR`, `TC`, `VT`, `DCT`, `node --test tests/bundle.test.mjs` in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards`, `node $HS --check` and `node $S --summary $PRE --json > $SP/summary-before.json`, and write each command with its last output line into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `TC` exits 0, `VT` reports 0 failed, `DCT` reports `fail 0`, the bundle test reports `fail 0`, `node $HS --check` exits 0 and `jq -r 'keys | join(\",\")' $SP/summary-before.json` prints the six runtimes.\n71: - [x] T002 Read how `$ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts` and `LCH` name the daemon socket under `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR`, and record whether two checkouts reach two daemons (`$SP/socket-key.txt`). Verify: the file names the function and the line that derive the socket name and ends with one word, `per-checkout` or `shared`. When it says `shared`, T016 gives each checkout its own socket directory.\n72: - [x] T003 Write `$SP/cold-start.mjs` and run it once with `--runs 5` (`$SP/cold-start-before.txt`). Each run makes a fresh directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cold-'))`, with `tmpdir` from `node:os`, pipes `{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"cwd\":\"<repository root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"cold-<n>\"}` into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory, and prints the milliseconds and the first line of `additionalContext` (or `<none>`). An optional `--warm` runs `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root <root> --format json --no-warm-only` detached with the same variable and waits 3,000 ms before the hook. After each run the script sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory, then removes the directory. The last line reads `fail-open N of 5`, where a run fails open when its first line does not start with `Advisor: live` or `Advisor: stale`. Verify: the file has six lines and its last line matches `fail-open [0-5] of 5`, `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cold-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing and `ls /tmp/system-skill-advisor | wc -l` prints the same number before and after the run. When N is 0, mark T024 to T026 `[x]` with `Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5` and the median milliseconds.\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n78: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n79: \n80: ### Wave 1\n81: - [x] T004 [P] Create `OF` with two exports. `parseOffer(head)` returns `{ offeredCommand, offeredPolicy }`: `offeredCommand` is the first match of `/\\/[a-z][a-z-]*:[a-z][a-z-]*(?: [a-z][a-z-]*)?/` in the head, or null, and `offeredPolicy` is `run`, `start` or `ask` when `(run)`, `(start)` or `(ask)` follows that match after optional spaces, or null. `replayOffer({ checkoutDir, prompt, sessionId, timeoutMs = 30000 })` runs `node <checkoutDir>/$HOOK` with `cwd` `checkoutDir` and the payload shape of T003, takes the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` and returns `parseOffer` of it with `offerError: null`, or null fields with `offerError` `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`. Create `OT` with cases for the heads `Advisor: live; use sk-git → /doctor:git hooks (ask) 0.82/0.12 pass.`, `Advisor: live; ambiguous: /doctor:git hooks 0.82/0.12 vs sk-git 0.86/0.16 pass.`, `Advisor: live; use command-spec-kit-plan 0.82/0.16 pass.` and a `replayOffer` call on a folder with no hook, which returns `offerError` `hook_missing`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n82: - [x] T005 [P] In `commandParts` (`S`), when the name holds whitespace, keep the text before the first space as `name` and the rest as `route`, so `/doctor:git hooks` looks up `doctor/git.md`. Add one case to `T`: events that read `.skilled/commands/doctor/git.md` and then write give `startState(events, { expected_command: '/doctor:git hooks', expected_policy: 'run' }).started` true. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed.\n83: - [x] T006 [P] In `apply` (`DI`), change the advisor flag to `enabled: options.promptAdvisor !== false`. In `DT`, rename the test to `prompt advisor stays on unless its row flag is false` and assert that `preStepCount({ adapters: { promptAdvisor: true } })` equals `preStepCount()` and that `preStepCount({ adapters: { promptAdvisor: false } })` is one lower. Verify: `rg -n \"promptAdvisor !== false\" $DI` prints one line, and `node --test tests/bundle.test.mjs` in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards` reports `fail 0`.\n84: - [x] T007 [P] Create `CK` and `CKT`. `CK [--root <dir>] [--config <path>] [--json]` reads `<root>/.codex/hooks.json` and prints `SKIP no-codex-hooks` with exit 0 when it is absent. It finds the `UserPromptSubmit` group `g` and hook index `i` whose `command` contains `hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js`, or prints `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent` with exit 1. It reads `--config`, else `${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml`, and looks for a header line `[hooks.state.\"<root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:<g>:<i>\"]`, with `<root>` as given or as its real path, followed by a `trusted_hash` line before the next header. Found prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` with exit 0. Otherwise it prints `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved <root>` and `repair: open /hooks in a Codex session at <root> and approve each entry`, with exit 1. A bad flag exits 2. It never prints a hash and calls no write, mkdir, rename or remove function. `CKT` covers an approved fixture, an unapproved fixture and a root with no `.codex`. Verify: `node --test $CKT` reports `pass 3` and `fail 0`, `rg -n \"writeFile|appendFile|mkdir|rename|rmSync|unlink\" $CK` prints nothing, and `shasum -a 256 ~/.codex/config.toml` prints the same digest before and after `node $CK --root .`, which prints one line starting `PASS` or `WARN`.\n85: - [x] T008 [P] Create `HW` and `HWT`. `HW --root <dir> [--json]` checks four runtimes: `claude` (`.claude/settings.json`, event `UserPromptSubmit`, marker `hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`), `codex` (`.codex/hooks.json`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js`), `cursor` (`.cursor/hooks.json`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js`) and `devin` (`.devin/hooks.v1.json`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js`). A runtime whose folder is absent is skipped. It reads the event under `hooks` or at the top level and prints `ok <runtime>` when its JSON text holds the marker, else `hook-missing <runtime> <file>`, also for a missing or unreadable file. It exits 1 when any line is `hook-missing`, 0 otherwise and 2 on a bad flag or a missing root. It writes nothing. `HWT` covers a root whose `.claude/settings.json` lacks the entry, the same root with it and a root with no runtime folder. Verify: `node --test $HWT` reports `pass 3` and `fail 0`, and `node $HW --root .` prints `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor` and `ok devin` and exits 0.\n86: - [x] T009 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the line about hyphenated commands: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved. Verify: `rg -n \"codex-hooks-approved\" $IG` prints one line and `rg -c \"trusted_hash\" $IG` prints 1.\n87: \n88: ### Wave 2\n89: - [ ] T010 [P] Add `briefDelivered({ runtime, locator, loadSession })` to `OF`. For `claude` it reads `locator.transcriptPath` and returns true when a line has `type` `attachment`, `attachment.type` `hook_additional_context`, `attachment.hookEvent` `UserPromptSubmit` and content matching `/Advisor: [a-z]+[;. ]/`, false when the file loads without one and `\"unknown\"` when it cannot be read. For `pi` it loads the session and tests its records with the same pattern. Every other runtime returns `\"unknown\"`. Add three `OT` cases: a Claude fixture with the attachment, one without it and a `devin` locator. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed.\n90: - [ ] T011 [P] In `S`, carry `wrote` (true when the run line's `changedPaths` is a non-empty array) on each scored result and add `byPolicy` to each tally block with keys `run`, `start` and `ask`, each `{ rows, capped, started, wrote }`, filled from the row's `expected_policy`. Print one text line per policy under each arm, `policy <name>: <rows> rows, <capped> capped, <started> started, <wrote> wrote`. Add one `T` case through the summary fixture. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.claude.pre.byPolicy | keys'` prints `[\"ask\",\"run\",\"start\"]`.\n91: - [ ] T012 [P] In `IG`, change `any of the six runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin or Pi` to `any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH)`, add DSH to the runtimes that spell commands with a hyphen and add one sentence: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`. Verify: `grep -ci dsh $IG` prints at least 2.\n92: - [ ] T013 [P] In `DR` section 5 and in the `prompt-advisor.mjs` row of `DA`, state that the bundle registers the prompt advisor unless its row flag is `false`, that the guards patch still writes `true` and that a lineage leaf stays without a brief. Verify: `rg -n \"unless its row flag is .false.\" $DR $DA` prints two lines and `rg -n \"Off unless\" $DA` prints nothing.\n93: - [ ] T014 [P] In `RMY`, add `codex_hook_approval: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs\"` to `upstream_assets` and one step after the `codex_hooks_installer` step: run `upstream_assets.codex_hook_approval` with `--root \"$PWD\"`. `PASS` is in sync, `WARN` sets STATUS to WARN and shows the repair line without counting as drift, and `SKIP` leaves STATUS unchanged. Keep every existing phrase. Verify: `rg -c \"codex_hook_approval\" $RMY` prints 2 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n94: - [ ] T015 [P] In `SCY`, add `hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"` to `upstream_assets`, add a step after the engine run that runs `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\"`, shows each `hook-missing <runtime>` line and ends with STATUS=WARN on exit 1, naming the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from Skilled's own file for that runtime into the target's file. Append to the invariant that the route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, keeping the words `check subcommand only`. Verify: `rg -c \"hook-wiring-check.cjs\" $SCY` prints at least 2 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n95: \n96: ### Wave 3\n97: - [ ] T016 [P] Add `backfillRunLog({ inPath, outPath, promptFor, replay = replayOffer, brief = briefDelivered, warm })` to `OF`. It refuses with code `same_path` when `outPath` resolves to `inPath`. It calls `promptFor(rowId)` for every line before writing, so a holdout or unknown row refuses the run with no output file. For each line it takes the checkout from `locator.projectDir`, warms each checkout once with `warm(checkoutDir)` (default: `advisor_status --workspace-root <dir> --format json --no-warm-only` through that checkout's `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`), replays the offer with session id `backfill-<rowId>`, sets `briefDelivered` and writes the line with the three fields and `offerBackfilled: true`. A line with no `projectDir` gets null fields and `offerError: 'no_checkout'`. When `$SP/socket-key.txt` says `shared`, `warm` and `replay` also set `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to one short `/tmp/ssa-bf-<n>` directory per checkout. Add `OT` cases with injected `replay`, `brief` and `warm` for a two-line log, a `no_checkout` line, a refused holdout id and `same_path`. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed.\n98: - [ ] T017 [P] In `S`, keep capped runs out of the start denominator: `startRows` and `started` count uncapped start rows only, and a new `cappedStartRows` counts capped start rows. Print `capped start rows <n>` on the arm line. Add one `T` case with a capped and an uncapped start row. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.opencode.pre | {startRate, cappedStartRows}'` prints a `startRate` whose denominator plus `cappedStartRows` equals the arm's start rows in `$SP/summary-before.json`.\n99: - [ ] T018 [P] In `$DS/README.markdown`, add `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` to the tree, the script table and the read-only table, each with its flags and exit codes. Verify: `rg -c \"codex-hook-approval-check.cjs|hook-wiring-check.cjs\" $DS/README.markdown` prints at least 4.\n100: \n101: ### Wave 4\n102: - [ ] T019 In `R`, import `replayOffer` and `briefDelivered` from `OF`. In `runTurn`, after the restore and before the line is appended, call `replayOffer({ checkoutDir: PROJECT_DIR, prompt: job.prompt, sessionId })` and add `offeredCommand` and `offeredPolicy` to the line, then add `briefDelivered` from the turn's locator (`\"unknown\"` in a dry run). Change nothing else in the turn. Verify: `node --check $R` exits 0, `rg -c \"offeredCommand|offeredPolicy|briefDelivered\" $R` prints at least 3, and `node $R --print-argv claude | jq -r 'type'` prints `array`.\n103: - [ ] T020 In `S`, add `offered`, `startedOfOffered` and `offerUnknown` to each tally block. `offered` counts uncapped start rows whose line's `offeredCommand` names the row's expected command by namespace and name, `startedOfOffered` counts the started ones among them and `offerUnknown` counts uncapped start rows whose line has no `offeredCommand` key. Print `offered <X>, started <Y> of <X>, offer unknown <n>` on the arm line. Add one `T` case with an offered and a not-offered start row. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '.claude.pre | {offered, startedOfOffered, offerUnknown}'` prints `{\"offered\":0,\"startedOfOffered\":0,\"offerUnknown\":12}`.\n104: \n105: ### Wave 5\n106: - [ ] T021 In `R`, add a `--backfill <run-log>` mode that needs `--out <new-log>` and calls `backfillRunLog` with a `promptFor` built from the runner's own `promptFor` and the fixture folder `resolve(dirname(<run-log>), G2_FIXTURE_DIRNAME)`. A refusal prints its code as JSON and exits 2. Add the mode to the usage text. Then write `$SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl` with two lines for row `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01`, runtime `claude`, arm `pre`, exit 0, empty `changedPaths`, the first with `locator` `{\"projectDir\":\"<absolute repository root>\"}` and the second with `locator` null, and run `node $R --backfill $SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl --out $SP/backfill-out.jsonl`. Verify: `jq -c '{offerBackfilled, briefDelivered, offerError, has: has(\"offeredCommand\")}' $SP/backfill-out.jsonl` prints `{\"offerBackfilled\":true,\"briefDelivered\":\"unknown\",\"offerError\":null,\"has\":true}` and then a line with `\"offerError\":\"no_checkout\"`, and `node $R --backfill $SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl --out $SP/backfill-fixture.jsonl` exits 2 and prints `same_path`.\n107: - [ ] T022 In `S`, after all lines are tallied, set `armIncomplete` on each runtime's arm block to true when its `runs` is lower than the largest `runs` of any runtime in the same arm, else false. End the arm's text line with `, arm incomplete` when it is true. Add one `T` case with two runtimes of two and one runs. Verify: `VT` reports 0 failed, and `node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '[to_entries[] | select(.value.pre.armIncomplete == true) | .key]'` prints the runtimes whose `pre` run count in `$SP/summary-before.json` is below the largest.\n108: \n109: ### Wave 6\n110: - [ ] T023 In `RA`, describe the three run-line fields and that the offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn, the `--backfill` mode and its refusals, and the summary keys `offered`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerUnknown`, `cappedStartRows`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`. Verify: `rg -c \"offeredCommand|--backfill|armIncomplete|byPolicy|cappedStartRows\" $RA` prints at least 5.\n111: \n112: ### Cold-start wave C1 (only when T003 shows a fail-open)\n113: - [x] T024 Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5 with a sandboxed socket (median 431 ms), and a true cold start with no daemon alive measured fail-open 0 of 5 (median 742 ms against the 2,500 ms hook budget, `scratch/cold-arena-result.txt`). Original task: [P] In `HR`, add a hook `advisor-warm` with concern `Start the skill advisor daemon at session start so the first prompt gets a brief`, bound for `claude` at `SessionStart` group 0 slot 8 and for `codex` at `SessionStart` group 0 slot 5, each with runner `node`, script `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, args `advisor_status --workspace-root . --format json --no-warm-only`, timeout 3 and fallback `background`. Run `node $HS`. Do not edit a generated file by hand. Verify: `node $HS --check` exits 0, `jq '[.hooks.SessionStart[].hooks[] | select(.command | test(\"skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status\"))] | length'` prints 1 for `.claude/settings.json` and for `.codex/hooks.json`, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- .cursor/hooks.json .devin/hooks.v1.json` prints nothing.\n114: - [x] T025 Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5 with a sandboxed socket (median 431 ms), and a true cold start with no daemon alive measured fail-open 0 of 5 (median 742 ms against the 2,500 ms hook budget, `scratch/cold-arena-result.txt`). Original task: [P] In `LCH`, set `SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS` to `750` in the daemon's environment when the launcher's own environment leaves it unset, and add the name to the list of variables passed to the daemon. Verify: `node --check $LCH` exits 0 and `rg -c \"SPECKIT_CASCADE_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS\" $LCH` prints at least 2.\n115: \n116: ### Cold-start wave C2\n117: - [x] T026 Dropped: T003 measured fail-open 0 of 5 with a sandboxed socket (median 431 ms), and a true cold start with no daemon alive measured fail-open 0 of 5 (median 742 ms against the 2,500 ms hook budget, `scratch/cold-arena-result.txt`). Original task: Run `node $SP/cold-start.mjs --runs 5 --warm` (`$SP/cold-start-after.txt`). Verify: its last line reads `fail-open 0 of 5`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cold-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing. If it reads more than 0, revert T024 and T025 and mark them `[B]` with the printed line.\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n123: ## Phase 3: Verification\n124: \n125: - [ ] T027 Run every gate. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `TC` exits 0, `VT` and `VO` report 0 failed, `node --test $CKT $HWT` and `DCT` report `fail 0`, `node --test tests/bundle.test.mjs` in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards` reports `fail 0` and `node $HS --check` exits 0.\n126: - [ ] T028 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .dsh | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing, and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .dsh INSTALL-SKILLED.md .claude .codex` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n127: - [ ] T029 [C] Backfill the before arm: run `node $R --backfill $PRE --out $SP/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl` from the repository root while the six arenas under `$TMPDIR/skilled-behaviour-arenas/pre-<runtime>` still exist at commit `2920b1abef`. Verify: `wc -l` prints the same number for both files, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- $PRE` exits 0 and `jq -r '\"\\(.runtime) \\(.briefDelivered)\"' $SP/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl | sort | uniq -c` shows every `claude` and `pi` line as `true` and every `codex`, `devin`, `opencode` and `dsh` line as `unknown`.\n128: - [ ] T030 [C] Run `node $S --summary $SP/runs-pre-attributed.jsonl > $SP/summary-attributed.txt`. Verify: every arm line holds `offered`, `capped start rows` and three `policy` lines, and a runtime with fewer rows than the others ends with `arm incomplete`.\n129: - [ ] T031 [C] Codex smoke: prepare one arena at this phase's commit, have the operator open `/hooks` in a Codex session there and approve each entry, then run one row through `R` with `--runtime codex --arm smoke`. Verify: `node $CK --root <arena>` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved`, and the rollout at the line's `locator.transcriptPath` contains `Advisor: `.\n130: - [ ] T032 Only when T031's rollout contains the brief: in `briefDelivered` (`OF`), decide `codex` from its raw rollout in the shape T031 shows, with one `OT` case built from that shape. Verify: `VO` reports 0 failed. When T031's rollout holds no brief, mark this task `[x]` with `Dropped: no Codex brief in the smoke rollout`.\n131: - [ ] T033 [C] DSH smoke: in an arena at this phase's commit, run one turn through `dsh` with one route patch and the guards patch and without the lineage patch. Verify: the stored step payload contains `Advisor: `.\n132: - [ ] T034 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n133: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n134: \n135: ---\n136: \n137: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n138: ## Completion Criteria\n139: \n140: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`, with T024 to T026 and T032 either done or marked dropped with their measured reason\n141: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n142: - [ ] The before arm is backfilled, and the attributed summary prints an offered count for every runtime\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n144: \n145: ---\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n148: ## Cross-References\n149: \n150: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n151: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n152: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n153: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n154: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: ## Verification Checklist\n159: \n160: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n161: ## Verification Protocol\n162: \n163: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n164: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n165: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n166: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n167: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n168: \n169: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n170: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n171: \n172: ---\n173: \n174: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n175: ## Pre-Implementation\n176: \n177: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers and the old-meaning summary are in `scratch/` (T001).\n178: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The coordinator confirmed the before arm is finished before wave 1 started.\n179: - [ ] CHK-003 [P1] The socket key and the cold-start measurement are recorded (T002, T003).\n180: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n185: ## Code Quality\n186: \n187: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0.\n188: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id (T028).\n189: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] The two check scripts and the backfill write nothing in the home folder (T007, T028).\n190: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A failed replay yields null fields with an `offerError`, never a crash (T004).\n191: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n196: ## Testing Checklist\n197: \n198: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] The scorer and offer tests pass (T027).\n199: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The floors hold (T027).\n200: - [ ] CHK-022 [P1] The doctor contract tests, the two check tests and the DSH bundle test pass (T027).\n201: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The backfill has as many lines as its input and leaves the input unchanged (T029).\n202: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n203: \n204: ---\n205: \n206: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n207: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n208: \n209: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `measurement`: the harness reports a rate it cannot attribute.\n210: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the start rate is listed: `rg -n \"startRate|startRows\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\n211: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Every runtime with a prompt hook file is in the hook-wiring table: claude, codex, cursor and devin.\n212: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n213: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n214: \n215: ---\n216: \n217: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n218: ## Security\n219: \n220: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task reads or prints holdout prompt text, and the backfill refuses a holdout row id (T016).\n221: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] The Codex check prints no hash value (T007).\n222: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n223: \n224: ---\n225: \n226: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n227: ## Documentation\n228: \n229: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same fields and numbers.\n230: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The install guide, the DSH READMEs, the doctor scripts README and the routing-accuracy README match the code (T009, T012, T013, T018, T023).\n231: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n232: \n233: ---\n234: \n235: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n236: ## File Organization\n237: \n238: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, fixtures, measurements and the attributed log live in `scratch/` only.\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n240: \n241: ---\n242: \n243: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n244: ## Verification Summary\n245: \n246: | Category | Total | Verified |\n247: |----------|-------|----------|\n248: | P0 Items | 11 | 0/11 |\n249: | P1 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n250: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n251: \n252: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n253: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528099951,"end":1794528099981}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794528102961,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","part":{"id":"prt_1d235ca31001Fw8PE7dv0GJfCP","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","messageID":"msg_1d235b2730017YCL4JatEGoGeg","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"522eba555a61dd4e7a8068073b56f478f2693a12","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":768,"output":90,"reasoning":10,"cache":{"read":16640,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794528106708,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","part":{"id":"prt_1d235d8d4001z6kfkBYjI9S71J","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","messageID":"msg_1d235ca36001CxixfPVpvLiCDv","type":"step-start","snapshot":"7269162469c4b709367a8eaf3c3b4dfc427ab855"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528108192,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","part":{"partID":"prt_1d235d8da002xibCrom3l7Gqyw","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","messageID":"msg_1d235ca36001CxixfPVpvLiCDv","type":"tool","id":"call_7bf1c098f6c4423abec7dc0b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md, lines 1-171\n1: # Repo Guards Plugin Bundle\n2: \n3: ---\n4: \n5: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n6: \n7: `repo-guards/` connects DSH events to the repository's shared guard cores. The entrypoint registers adapters, and each adapter translates event data into a core call and delivers the result. Shared cores keep policy ownership.\n8: \n9: The bundle runs in two compositions. An interactive session, `dsh web` or a headless run with only the guards patch, gets every adapter. A fan-out leaf adds the lineage patch, and its marker row turns off the four adapters that write state or start background work. Everything else, the guards, the context injections and decision capture, runs in both.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n14: \n15: ```text\n16: ╭──────────────────────╮\n17: │ DSH event            │\n18: ╰──────────┬───────────╯\n19:            ▼\n20: ┌──────────────────────┐\n21: │ index.mjs            │\n22: │ registers adapters   │\n23: └──────────┬───────────┘\n24:            ▼\n25: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n26: │ adapters/*.mjs (links)       │\n27: │ -> .skilled/hooks/<c>/dsh/   │\n28: │ -> <skill>/hooks/dsh/        │\n29: └──────────┬───────────────────┘\n30:            ▼\n31: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n32: │ Shared hooks and runtimes    │\n33: │ policy and context cores     │\n34: └──────────┬───────────────────┘\n35:            ▼\n36: ╭───────────────────────────────╮\n37: │ inject, attach, allow or deny │\n38: ╰───────────────────────────────╯\n39: ```\n40: \n41: Dependency direction: `index.mjs` → adapter links → real adapters → shared hooks and runtime cores. Adapters own DSH event wiring and result delivery. They do not copy policy from shared cores.\n42: \n43: ### Adapter layout\n44: \n45: DSH uses the layout Pi uses. Every file in `adapters/` is a relative link to the real adapter in the hook library: `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` for the portable concerns, or the owning skill's `hooks/dsh/` folder for spec-gate, completion, session lifecycle, the skill advisor and the two sk-git adapters, each with an index link in `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/`. Node resolves a link to its real path before it resolves the adapter's own imports, so each adapter's imports are written for its real folder. The adapters that find the checkout from their own file count up from that folder.\n46: \n47: `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` runs, expects one link here per `.mjs` file in a `dsh/` folder of the hook library and reports a missing link, a stale one or a real file in its place. Add an adapter by writing it into its `dsh/` folder, then run the synchronizer without `--check` to create the link.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. DIRECTORY TREE\n52: \n53: ```text\n54: repo-guards/\n55: +-- index.mjs                 # bundle entry the guards patch loads\n56: +-- lineage-leaf.mjs          # marker plugin the lineage patch inserts\n57: +-- adapters/                 # one relative link per adapter, see section 2\n58: |   +-- ask-surface-guard.mjs, classifier-injection-screen.mjs, completion-evidence.mjs\n59: |   +-- decision-capture.mjs\n60: |   +-- dispatch-audit.mjs, dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs, env-secret-guard.mjs, git-message-gate.mjs\n61: |   +-- git-preflight-advisory.mjs, goal-context.mjs, goal-manage.mjs\n62: |   +-- mcp-route-guard.mjs, overlay-guard.mjs, post-edit-quality.mjs, prompt-advisor.mjs\n63: |   +-- session-compact-context.mjs, session-start-advisories.mjs, session-start-context.mjs\n64: |   +-- session-stop-context.mjs, spec-gate-classify.mjs, spec-gate-enforce.mjs\n65: |   +-- task-dispatch-guard.mjs\n66: |   `-- dsh-llm.mjs, session-role.mjs (shared helpers in .skilled/hooks/shared/dsh/)\n67: +-- tests/\n68: |   `-- bundle.test.mjs       # patches, lineage-leaf plugin, advisor row flag, adapter links\n69: `-- README.md\n70: ```\n71: \n72: Each adapter's tests sit in its concern's `tests/` folder as `dsh-<concern>.test.mjs`, such as `.skilled/hooks/goal/tests/dsh-goal.test.mjs`. The prompt advisor's are in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/`. They share the fake plugin context in `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/dsh-plugin-harness.mjs`.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 4. ADAPTER POLICIES\n77: \n78: | Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Leaf | Error policy |\n79: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n80: | `dispatch-audit` | `tools/post-execute` | `bash` | runs | Log and continue |\n81: | `dispatch-preflight-lint` | `tools/pre-execute` | `bash` | runs | Log and deny on core failure |\n82: | `spec-gate-classify` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | runs, off by the runner's `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1` | Log and continue |\n83: | `spec-gate-enforce` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `bash` | runs, off by the runner's `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1` | Log and deny on core failure |\n84: | `completion-evidence` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn | runs | Log and continue |\n85: | `ask-surface-guard` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn: a closing typed option menu with no `ask_user_question` call | skipped, as is any headless or child session, since none has a question tool | Log and continue |\n86: | `task-dispatch-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `subagent`, `subagent_fork` | runs | Log and continue |\n87: | `post-edit-quality` | `tools/post-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | runs | Log and continue |\n88: | `mcp-route-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `mcp__*` | runs | Log and deny on core failure, and deny a `code_mode` tool outside `call_tool_chain`, `list_tools`, `search_tools` and `tool_info` |\n89: | `classifier-injection-screen` | `tools/post-execute` | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `mcp__*` | runs | Log and continue |\n90: | `overlay-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a path an overlay owns |\n91: | `env-secret-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `read`, `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `grep`, `bash` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a call that reads or writes a dotenv file |\n92: | `git-preflight-advisory` | `tools/post-execute` | Bash Git commands | runs | Log and continue, add context |\n93: | `git-message-gate` | `tools/pre-execute` | Bash commands covered by the message contract | runs | Log unexpected errors and continue, deny on `ContractError` |\n94: | `goal-context` | `agent/created` | `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` chat slice | runs | Log and continue |\n95: | `session-start-context` | `agent/created` | Session-prime output | runs | Log and continue |\n96: | `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | runs | Log and continue |\n97: | `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | runs, headless has no question tool | Log and continue |\n98: | `prompt-advisor` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | off | Log and continue |\n99: | `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | off | Log and continue |\n100: | `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | off | Log each failing guard and continue |\n101: | `session-stop-context` | `agent/disposed` | `session-stop.js` autosave | off | Log and continue |\n102: \n103: Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`. Their core errors do not block tool calls. They build injected messages and the goal tool with the harness's own `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`, which `dsh-llm.mjs` resolves from the running `dsh` binary, because this checkout has no copy of them.\n104: \n105: `dispatch-audit`, `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `git-preflight-advisory`, `mcp-route-guard` and `session-start-advisories` find the checkout from their own file, not the session cwd. A dsh session runs in a lineage or scratch folder, where a cwd-relative rule tree would be empty and the lint would allow every command. `git-message-gate` is a policy gate, so a contract violation or unreadable contract returns `deny`.\n106: \n107: `goal-manage` and `session-compact-context` wait for the `commands`, `tools` and `agents` services through `ctx.inject`. A bundle-level `inject` would hold every guard until those services exist, and this cordis build has no optional form.\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ## 5. CONFIGURATION\n112: \n113: The guards patch turns the prompt advisor on. The lineage patch keeps it off for a fan-out leaf through its marker row, so the flag stays `true` in both compositions.\n114: \n115: ```yaml\n116: - id: repo-guards\n117:   name: ../plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\n118:   config:\n119:     adapters:\n120:       promptAdvisor: true\n121: ```\n122: \n123: Set `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` to a packet directory, relative to the DSH workspace or as an absolute path inside it. The goal core reads the packet goal and returns its `chatSlice`, which matches the `chat_slice` from `goal.cjs packet`. The adapter injects that string only, without goal frontmatter.\n124: \n125: In an interactive session, `/goal-dsh` and the `dsh_goal` tool run the shared manage CLI under this session's scope. The tool takes the OpenCode action set: `set`, `bind`, `unbind`, `resent`, `log`, `packet`, `show`, `clear`, `complete`, `pause`, `history`, `resume`, `doctor` and `health`. The command passes its words to the same CLI, so `/goal-dsh bind <packet>` or `/goal-dsh log <item> | <state> | <evidence>` work as written, and a bare `/goal-dsh` shows the goal. `OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED=1` turns the whole goal surface off.\n126: \n127: Each session-start guard answers to its own switch: `SYSTEM_GIT_WORKTREE_GUARD_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_GIT_HOOKS_CHECK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_LIVE_FOLLOW_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_DIST_FRESHNESS_DISABLED` and `SYSTEM_HOOK_INSTALL_DISABLED`. `SYSTEM_SESSION_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED` turns off all session-lifecycle adapters.\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: ## 6. VALIDATION\n132: \n133: Run these commands from the repository root.\n134: \n135: ```sh\n136: node --test .skilled/hooks/*/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/\n137: ```\n138: \n139: Expected result: 90 tests pass.\n140: \n141: ```sh\n142: node --test .skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-dsh.test.mjs\n143: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check\n144: ```\n145: \n146: Expected result: 8 sweep tests pass, and the mirror check prints `PASS` with the `dsh-adapters` tree among its trees.\n147: \n148: The Git message adapter also uses the fixtures in the shared contract suite:\n149: \n150: ```sh\n151: node --test .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.test.mjs\n152: ```\n153: \n154: Expected result: 38 tests pass.\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: ## 7. RELATED\n159: \n160: - [Guard patch](../../patches/guards.patch.yml) and [lineage patch](../../patches/lineage.patch.yml)\n161: - [Hook library](../../../.skilled/hooks/README.md), whose coverage matrix carries the DSH column\n162: - [Goal core](../../../.skilled/hooks/goal/lib/goal-core.cjs)\n163: - [DSH session sweep](../../../.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-dsh.mjs)\n164: - [Git message contract tests](../../../.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.test.mjs)\n165: \n166: <!-- readme-check\n167: allow-ref hooks/dsh/ | a folder name inside each owning skill, not a path from here; the same sentence names the full paths\n168: allow-ref ../plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs | a path inside a patch file, resolved from .dsh/patches/, not from this README\n169: allow-count 90 tests | node --test prints this total; no file listing can derive it\n170: allow-count 38 tests | node --test prints this total; no file listing can derive it\n171: -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md, lines 1-171\n1: # Repo Guards Plugin Bundle\n2: \n3: ---\n4: \n5: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n6: \n7: `repo-guards/` connects DSH events to the repository's shared guard cores. The entrypoint registers adapters, and each adapter translates event data into a core call and delivers the result. Shared cores keep policy ownership.\n8: \n9: The bundle runs in two compositions. An interactive session, `dsh web` or a headless run with only the guards patch, gets every adapter. A fan-out leaf adds the lineage patch, and its marker row turns off the four adapters that write state or start background work. Everything else, the guards, the context injections and decision capture, runs in both.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n14: \n15: ```text\n16: ╭──────────────────────╮\n17: │ DSH event            │\n18: ╰──────────┬───────────╯\n19:            ▼\n20: ┌──────────────────────┐\n21: │ index.mjs            │\n22: │ registers adapters   │\n23: └──────────┬───────────┘\n24:            ▼\n25: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n26: │ adapters/*.mjs (links)       │\n27: │ -> .skilled/hooks/<c>/dsh/   │\n28: │ -> <skill>/hooks/dsh/        │\n29: └──────────┬───────────────────┘\n30:            ▼\n31: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n32: │ Shared hooks and runtimes    │\n33: │ policy and context cores     │\n34: └──────────┬───────────────────┘\n35:            ▼\n36: ╭───────────────────────────────╮\n37: │ inject, attach, allow or deny │\n38: ╰───────────────────────────────╯\n39: ```\n40: \n41: Dependency direction: `index.mjs` → adapter links → real adapters → shared hooks and runtime cores. Adapters own DSH event wiring and result delivery. They do not copy policy from shared cores.\n42: \n43: ### Adapter layout\n44: \n45: DSH uses the layout Pi uses. Every file in `adapters/` is a relative link to the real adapter in the hook library: `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` for the portable concerns, or the owning skill's `hooks/dsh/` folder for spec-gate, completion, session lifecycle, the skill advisor and the two sk-git adapters, each with an index link in `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/`. Node resolves a link to its real path before it resolves the adapter's own imports, so each adapter's imports are written for its real folder. The adapters that find the checkout from their own file count up from that folder.\n46: \n47: `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` runs, expects one link here per `.mjs` file in a `dsh/` folder of the hook library and reports a missing link, a stale one or a real file in its place. Add an adapter by writing it into its `dsh/` folder, then run the synchronizer without `--check` to create the link.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. DIRECTORY TREE\n52: \n53: ```text\n54: repo-guards/\n55: +-- index.mjs                 # bundle entry the guards patch loads\n56: +-- lineage-leaf.mjs          # marker plugin the lineage patch inserts\n57: +-- adapters/                 # one relative link per adapter, see section 2\n58: |   +-- ask-surface-guard.mjs, classifier-injection-screen.mjs, completion-evidence.mjs\n59: |   +-- decision-capture.mjs\n60: |   +-- dispatch-audit.mjs, dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs, env-secret-guard.mjs, git-message-gate.mjs\n61: |   +-- git-preflight-advisory.mjs, goal-context.mjs, goal-manage.mjs\n62: |   +-- mcp-route-guard.mjs, overlay-guard.mjs, post-edit-quality.mjs, prompt-advisor.mjs\n63: |   +-- session-compact-context.mjs, session-start-advisories.mjs, session-start-context.mjs\n64: |   +-- session-stop-context.mjs, spec-gate-classify.mjs, spec-gate-enforce.mjs\n65: |   +-- task-dispatch-guard.mjs\n66: |   `-- dsh-llm.mjs, session-role.mjs (shared helpers in .skilled/hooks/shared/dsh/)\n67: +-- tests/\n68: |   `-- bundle.test.mjs       # patches, lineage-leaf plugin, advisor row flag, adapter links\n69: `-- README.md\n70: ```\n71: \n72: Each adapter's tests sit in its concern's `tests/` folder as `dsh-<concern>.test.mjs`, such as `.skilled/hooks/goal/tests/dsh-goal.test.mjs`. The prompt advisor's are in `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/`. They share the fake plugin context in `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/dsh-plugin-harness.mjs`.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 4. ADAPTER POLICIES\n77: \n78: | Adapter | DSH event | Scope | Leaf | Error policy |\n79: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n80: | `dispatch-audit` | `tools/post-execute` | `bash` | runs | Log and continue |\n81: | `dispatch-preflight-lint` | `tools/pre-execute` | `bash` | runs | Log and deny on core failure |\n82: | `spec-gate-classify` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | runs, off by the runner's `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1` | Log and continue |\n83: | `spec-gate-enforce` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `bash` | runs, off by the runner's `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1` | Log and deny on core failure |\n84: | `completion-evidence` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn | runs | Log and continue |\n85: | `ask-surface-guard` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Current assistant turn: a closing typed option menu with no `ask_user_question` call | skipped, as is any headless or child session, since none has a question tool | Log and continue |\n86: | `task-dispatch-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `subagent`, `subagent_fork` | runs | Log and continue |\n87: | `post-edit-quality` | `tools/post-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | runs | Log and continue |\n88: | `mcp-route-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `mcp__*` | runs | Log and deny on core failure, and deny a `code_mode` tool outside `call_tool_chain`, `list_tools`, `search_tools` and `tool_info` |\n89: | `classifier-injection-screen` | `tools/post-execute` | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `mcp__*` | runs | Log and continue |\n90: | `overlay-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a path an overlay owns |\n91: | `env-secret-guard` | `tools/pre-execute` | `read`, `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch`, `grep`, `bash` | runs | Log and allow, deny only a call that reads or writes a dotenv file |\n92: | `git-preflight-advisory` | `tools/post-execute` | Bash Git commands | runs | Log and continue, add context |\n93: | `git-message-gate` | `tools/pre-execute` | Bash commands covered by the message contract | runs | Log unexpected errors and continue, deny on `ContractError` |\n94: | `goal-context` | `agent/created` | `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` chat slice | runs | Log and continue |\n95: | `session-start-context` | `agent/created` | Session-prime output | runs | Log and continue |\n96: | `session-compact-context` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Session-prime `compact` output | runs | Log and continue |\n97: | `decision-capture` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | `ask_user_question` answers and late timed replies | runs, headless has no question tool | Log and continue |\n98: | `prompt-advisor` | `agent/pre-step` | Latest operator prompt | off | Log and continue |\n99: | `goal-manage` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | `/goal-dsh`, `dsh_goal`, goal brief, verify note | off | Log and continue |\n100: | `session-start-advisories` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | The six warn-only session-start guards | off | Log each failing guard and continue |\n101: | `session-stop-context` | `agent/disposed` | `session-stop.js` autosave | off | Log and continue |\n102: \n103: Context adapters call `agent.inject` or return `additionalContexts`. Their core errors do not block tool calls. They build injected messages and the goal tool with the harness's own `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`, which `dsh-llm.mjs` resolves from the running `dsh` binary, because this checkout has no copy of them.\n104: \n105: `dispatch-audit`, `dispatch-preflight-lint`, `git-preflight-advisory`, `mcp-route-guard` and `session-start-advisories` find the checkout from their own file, not the session cwd. A dsh session runs in a lineage or scratch folder, where a cwd-relative rule tree would be empty and the lint would allow every command. `git-message-gate` is a policy gate, so a contract violation or unreadable contract returns `deny`.\n106: \n107: `goal-manage` and `session-compact-context` wait for the `commands`, `tools` and `agents` services through `ctx.inject`. A bundle-level `inject` would hold every guard until those services exist, and this cordis build has no optional form.\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ## 5. CONFIGURATION\n112: \n113: The guards patch turns the prompt advisor on. The lineage patch keeps it off for a fan-out leaf through its marker row, so the flag stays `true` in both compositions.\n114: \n115: ```yaml\n116: - id: repo-guards\n117:   name: ../plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs\n118:   config:\n119:     adapters:\n120:       promptAdvisor: true\n121: ```\n122: \n123: Set `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` to a packet directory, relative to the DSH workspace or as an absolute path inside it. The goal core reads the packet goal and returns its `chatSlice`, which matches the `chat_slice` from `goal.cjs packet`. The adapter injects that string only, without goal frontmatter.\n124: \n125: In an interactive session, `/goal-dsh` and the `dsh_goal` tool run the shared manage CLI under this session's scope. The tool takes the OpenCode action set: `set`, `bind`, `unbind`, `resent`, `log`, `packet`, `show`, `clear`, `complete`, `pause`, `history`, `resume`, `doctor` and `health`. The command passes its words to the same CLI, so `/goal-dsh bind <packet>` or `/goal-dsh log <item> | <state> | <evidence>` work as written, and a bare `/goal-dsh` shows the goal. `OPENCODE_GOAL_DISABLED=1` turns the whole goal surface off.\n126: \n127: Each session-start guard answers to its own switch: `SYSTEM_GIT_WORKTREE_GUARD_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_GIT_HOOKS_CHECK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_PRIMARY_RECONCILE_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_LIVE_FOLLOW_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_DIST_FRESHNESS_DISABLED` and `SYSTEM_HOOK_INSTALL_DISABLED`. `SYSTEM_SESSION_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED` turns off all session-lifecycle adapters.\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: ## 6. VALIDATION\n132: \n133: Run these commands from the repository root.\n134: \n135: ```sh\n136: node --test .skilled/hooks/*/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/\n137: ```\n138: \n139: Expected result: 90 tests pass.\n140: \n141: ```sh\n142: node --test .skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-dsh.test.mjs\n143: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check\n144: ```\n145: \n146: Expected result: 8 sweep tests pass, and the mirror check prints `PASS` with the `dsh-adapters` tree among its trees.\n147: \n148: The Git message adapter also uses the fixtures in the shared contract suite:\n149: \n150: ```sh\n151: node --test .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.test.mjs\n152: ```\n153: \n154: Expected result: 38 tests pass.\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: ## 7. RELATED\n159: \n160: - [Guard patch](../../patches/guards.patch.yml) and [lineage patch](../../patches/lineage.patch.yml)\n161: - [Hook library](../../../.skilled/hooks/README.md), whose coverage matrix carries the DSH column\n162: - [Goal core](../../../.skilled/hooks/goal/lib/goal-core.cjs)\n163: - [DSH session sweep](../../../.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-dsh.mjs)\n164: - [Git message contract tests](../../../.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.test.mjs)\n165: \n166: <!-- readme-check\n167: allow-ref hooks/dsh/ | a folder name inside each owning skill, not a path from here; the same sentence names the full paths\n168: allow-ref ../plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs | a path inside a patch file, resolved from .dsh/patches/, not from this README\n169: allow-count 90 tests | node --test prints this total; no file listing can derive it\n170: allow-count 38 tests | node --test prints this total; no file listing can derive it\n171: -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528106714,"end":1794528108192}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528108217,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","part":{"partID":"prt_1d235d8db001wq1XlJfRrYcQ8S","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb12d3ffevysEI5uvl2ewzH","messageID":"msg_1d235ca36001CxixfPVpvLiCDv","type":"tool","id":"call_d47a2226b3434bd2a134687e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Repo Guards Adapters: One Link per DSH Adapter\"\n3: description: \"Relative links from the repo-guards bundle to every DSH adapter in the hook library and the owning skills.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"repo guards adapters\"\n6:   - \"dsh adapter links\"\n7:   - \"dsh guard registration\"\n8: version: 1.0.1.0\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Repo Guards Adapters: One Link per DSH Adapter\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: `adapters/` holds one relative symlink per DSH adapter that the `repo-guards` bundle registers. Each link points at the real adapter in `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` or in an owning skill's `hooks/dsh/` folder. Node resolves a link to its real path before it resolves the file's own imports, so every adapter's imports are written for its real folder. `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` expects one link here per `.mjs` file in a `dsh/` folder of the hook library.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 2. WHAT EACH FILE DOES\n22: \n23: | File | Event or role | What it does | On error |\n24: |---|---|---|---|\n25: | `classifier-injection-screen.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on `web_fetch`, `web_search` and `mcp__*` | Screens fetched text with the shared classifier advisory and adds the warnings to the tool result. | Fails open. `ERROR_POLICY` is `fail-open`. |\n26: | `completion-evidence.mjs` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Holds a completion claim in the ending reply to its evidence with the shared sentinel. Advisory only. | Fails open. |\n27: | `decision-capture.mjs` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | Captures `ask_user_question` answers and late replies into the record queue. | Fails open. The save-time sweep recovers missed records. |\n28: | `dispatch-audit.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on `bash` | Records dispatch audit rows under the checkout's log path. | Fails open. |\n29: | `dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `bash` | Runs the dispatch rule checks and denies a command the core rejects. | Fails closed. A core failure denies the command. |\n30: | `dsh-llm.mjs` | Shared loader, no event | Loads `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` from the running `dsh` binary and caches each module. | A load failure rejects to the calling adapter. |\n31: | `env-secret-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on every tool | Denies a file tool or shell command that reads or writes a dotenv file, naming the value-free CLI in the reason. | Fails open. A core failure is logged and the call proceeds. |\n32: | `git-message-gate.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on Bash commands covered by the message contract | Checks the commit message contract and denies on a `ContractError`. | Logs an unexpected error and continues. A `ContractError` denies. |\n33: | `git-preflight-advisory.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on Git Bash commands | Adds up to three Git preflight advisories to the result. | Fails open. |\n34: | `goal-context.mjs` | `agent/created` | Injects the `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` goal chat slice. | Fails open. |\n35: | `goal-manage.mjs` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | Registers `/goal-dsh` and `dsh_goal`, injects the goal brief, records the turn and delivers the verify note on idle. | Fails open. A fan-out leaf keeps the surface off. |\n36: | `mcp-route-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `mcp__*` | Enforces MCP routing and denies a `code_mode` tool outside `call_tool_chain`, `list_tools`, `search_tools` and `tool_info`. | Fails closed. |\n37: | `overlay-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `write`, `edit` and `apply_patch` | Denies a path an overlay owns and allows a path it cannot judge. | Fails open. |\n38: | `post-edit-quality.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on `write`, `edit` and `apply_patch` | Runs the post-edit quality router and adds its findings to the result. | Fails open. |\n39: | `prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/created`, `session/event`, `agent/pre-step` | Runs the Skill Advisor and adds the brief to the step. Off unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true. | Fails open. |\n40: | `session-compact-context.mjs` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Re-primes the agent after a completed compaction with the session-prime `compact` source. | Fails open. A failed compaction gets nothing. |\n41: | `session-role.mjs` | Shared helper, no event | Reads and writes the process-wide lineage-leaf marker on `Symbol.for('skilled.repo-guards.lineage-leaf')`. | No error path. A missing marker reads as false. |\n42: | `session-start-advisories.mjs` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | Runs the warn-only session-start guards from this checkout and injects one notice with their warnings. | Fails open per guard. |\n43: | `session-start-context.mjs` | `agent/created` | Injects `session-prime.js` output for a startup or resumed session and exports `runSessionPrime`. | Fails open. |\n44: | `session-stop-context.mjs` | `agent/disposed` | Runs `session-stop.js` with the Stop payload and injects nothing. | Fails open. An autosave failure never blocks close. |\n45: | `spec-gate-classify.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` | Runs the shared Gate-3 classifier on the operator prompt and adds the deferral notice to the step. | Fails open. |\n46: | `spec-gate-enforce.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` and `bash` | Asks at the first undelivered write or edit and denies by the shared verdict. | Fails closed. |\n47: | `task-dispatch-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `subagent` and `subagent_fork` | Records deep-loop warnings and audits, then passes the call. | Fails open. |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. RELATED\n52: \n53: - [`../README.md`](../README.md): the bundle, its adapter policy table and its validation commands.\n54: - [`../index.mjs`](../index.mjs): the bundle entry that registers these adapters.\n55: - [`../lineage-leaf.mjs`](../lineage-leaf.mjs): the marker plugin the lineage patch inserts.\n56: - [`../../../../.skilled/hooks/README.md`](../../../../.skilled/hooks/README.md): the hook library and its coverage matrix.\n57: \n58: <!-- readme-check\n59: allow-ref hooks/dsh/ | a folder name inside each owning skill, not a path from here; the same sentence names the full path form\n60: -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Repo Guards Adapters: One Link per DSH Adapter\"\n3: description: \"Relative links from the repo-guards bundle to every DSH adapter in the hook library and the owning skills.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"repo guards adapters\"\n6:   - \"dsh adapter links\"\n7:   - \"dsh guard registration\"\n8: version: 1.0.1.0\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Repo Guards Adapters: One Link per DSH Adapter\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: `adapters/` holds one relative symlink per DSH adapter that the `repo-guards` bundle registers. Each link points at the real adapter in `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` or in an owning skill's `hooks/dsh/` folder. Node resolves a link to its real path before it resolves the file's own imports, so every adapter's imports are written for its real folder. `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` expects one link here per `.mjs` file in a `dsh/` folder of the hook library.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 2. WHAT EACH FILE DOES\n22: \n23: | File | Event or role | What it does | On error |\n24: |---|---|---|---|\n25: | `classifier-injection-screen.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on `web_fetch`, `web_search` and `mcp__*` | Screens fetched text with the shared classifier advisory and adds the warnings to the tool result. | Fails open. `ERROR_POLICY` is `fail-open`. |\n26: | `completion-evidence.mjs` | `agent/turn-stopping` | Holds a completion claim in the ending reply to its evidence with the shared sentinel. Advisory only. | Fails open. |\n27: | `decision-capture.mjs` | `tools/result`, `session/event`, `agent/status` | Captures `ask_user_question` answers and late replies into the record queue. | Fails open. The save-time sweep recovers missed records. |\n28: | `dispatch-audit.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on `bash` | Records dispatch audit rows under the checkout's log path. | Fails open. |\n29: | `dispatch-preflight-lint.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `bash` | Runs the dispatch rule checks and denies a command the core rejects. | Fails closed. A core failure denies the command. |\n30: | `dsh-llm.mjs` | Shared loader, no event | Loads `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` from the running `dsh` binary and caches each module. | A load failure rejects to the calling adapter. |\n31: | `env-secret-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on every tool | Denies a file tool or shell command that reads or writes a dotenv file, naming the value-free CLI in the reason. | Fails open. A core failure is logged and the call proceeds. |\n32: | `git-message-gate.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on Bash commands covered by the message contract | Checks the commit message contract and denies on a `ContractError`. | Logs an unexpected error and continues. A `ContractError` denies. |\n33: | `git-preflight-advisory.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on Git Bash commands | Adds up to three Git preflight advisories to the result. | Fails open. |\n34: | `goal-context.mjs` | `agent/created` | Injects the `DSH_SPEC_FOLDER` goal chat slice. | Fails open. |\n35: | `goal-manage.mjs` | `agent/created`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping`, `agent/status` | Registers `/goal-dsh` and `dsh_goal`, injects the goal brief, records the turn and delivers the verify note on idle. | Fails open. A fan-out leaf keeps the surface off. |\n36: | `mcp-route-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `mcp__*` | Enforces MCP routing and denies a `code_mode` tool outside `call_tool_chain`, `list_tools`, `search_tools` and `tool_info`. | Fails closed. |\n37: | `overlay-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `write`, `edit` and `apply_patch` | Denies a path an overlay owns and allows a path it cannot judge. | Fails open. |\n38: | `post-edit-quality.mjs` | `tools/post-execute` on `write`, `edit` and `apply_patch` | Runs the post-edit quality router and adds its findings to the result. | Fails open. |\n39: | `prompt-advisor.mjs` | `agent/created`, `session/event`, `agent/pre-step` | Runs the Skill Advisor and adds the brief to the step. Off unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is true. | Fails open. |\n40: | `session-compact-context.mjs` | `session/event` (`compaction/end`) | Re-primes the agent after a completed compaction with the session-prime `compact` source. | Fails open. A failed compaction gets nothing. |\n41: | `session-role.mjs` | Shared helper, no event | Reads and writes the process-wide lineage-leaf marker on `Symbol.for('skilled.repo-guards.lineage-leaf')`. | No error path. A missing marker reads as false. |\n42: | `session-start-advisories.mjs` | `agent/created` (`startup`) | Runs the warn-only session-start guards from this checkout and injects one notice with their warnings. | Fails open per guard. |\n43: | `session-start-context.mjs` | `agent/created` | Injects `session-prime.js` output for a startup or resumed session and exports `runSessionPrime`. | Fails open. |\n44: | `session-stop-context.mjs` | `agent/disposed` | Runs `session-stop.js` with the Stop payload and injects nothing. | Fails open. An autosave failure never blocks close. |\n45: | `spec-gate-classify.mjs` | `agent/pre-step` | Runs the shared Gate-3 classifier on the operator prompt and adds the deferral notice to the step. | Fails open. |\n46: | `spec-gate-enforce.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `write`, `edit`, `apply_patch` and `bash` | Asks at the first undelivered write or edit and denies by the shared verdict. | Fails closed. |\n47: | `task-dispatch-guard.mjs` | `tools/pre-execute` on `subagent` and `subagent_fork` | Records deep-loop warnings and audits, then passes the call. | Fails open. |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 3. RELATED\n52: \n53: - [`../README.md`](../README.md): the bundle, its adapter policy table and its validation commands.\n54: - [`../index.mjs`](../index.mjs): the bundle entry that registers these adapters.\n55: - [`../lineage-leaf.mjs`](../lineage-leaf.mjs): the marker plugin the lineage patch inserts.\n56: - [`../../../../.skilled/hooks/README.md`](../../../../.skilled/hooks/README.md): the hook library and its coverage matrix.\n57: \n58: <!-- readme-check\n59: allow-ref hooks/dsh/ | a folder name inside each owning skill, not a path from here; the same sentence names the full path form\n60: -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794528106715,"end":1794528108217}}}}
